decisions:
  - id: d1
    decision: Logger gets independent patch bump (3.5.1 → 3.5.2) instead of jumping to 5.38.1
    rationale: Logger has its own cadence (3.x). Jumping version numbers arbitrarily to match paradigm CLI would be misleading. Per semver, patch bump for exports-metadata-only fix is correct.
  - id: d2
    decision: Scoped .gitignore pattern with explicit sql.js.d.ts negation instead of blanket .d.ts block in src/
    rationale: Three intentional hand-authored sql.js.d.ts stubs exist in paradigm / sentinel / paradigm-mcp (typed shim for a library without native types). Blanket ignore would stop tracking them; explicit negation preserves intent while catching future tsup output leakage.
  - id: d3
    decision: v6.0 pack manifest = pack.yaml at pack root, not a package.json field
    rationale: Manifests exceed 40 lines (branding, theme, compliance). Consistent with Paradigm house style (portal.yaml, .paradigm/config.yaml, roster.yaml).
  - id: d4
    decision: v6.0 decision-store canonical = .paradigm/decisions/TD-*.yaml (streams), absorbing ADR fields from wisdom-decisions
    rationale: Richer participant-stance schema, already integrated with paradigm_decision_* tools, higher on-disk cardinality. Cleaner than retaining parallel ADR store.
  - id: d5
    decision: v6.0 lore.type='decision' becomes HARD error, wisdom.type='decision' stays as soft deprecation
    rationale: Asymmetry is deliberate. lore's decision type was the three-way fracture offender Loid flagged. wisdom's is the cleaner legacy path; can soft-deprecate for one minor. Flagged to user for symmetry preference.
learnings:
  - 'Cleanup audits produce false positives at ~20% rate. 5 of 26 findings from this audit were false positives (sentinel-web exports already correct, README didn''t contain ''v2.0'', umbrella dirs are thin by design, VSCode doesn''t need engines.node, .next/ already scoped-ignored). Reviewer triage caught them in ~1h. Lesson: always triage audits before acting; don''t trust raw audit output as work items.'
  - Build artifacts in src/ directories are a pattern worth policing with .gitignore preemptively, not just cleanup. The 4 stray tool-cache.* files had been committed at an unknown prior date and silently grew. Scoped pattern catches all future occurrences across all packages.
  - Version bump rules need carving out for packages with independent cadence. Memory had explicit rules for paradigm / paradigm-mcp / sentinel / university but not logger. Logger is a published package with its own version lineage; bumping to 5.38.1 would have broken its semver narrative. Patch bump on the logger package itself is the correct call.
  - 'Architect-as-subagent (paradigm:architect) doesn''t have Write tool access. Large specs must be returned as final-message text and written by the parent agent. Architect''s 700-line spec returned in a persisted-output file; parent had to extract and write. Future: when dispatching architect for spec writing, either grant Write or plan for the text-return bridge.'
